# R11: Mayor Somerton comes out to greet Lord Phillip once the Round is quiet. Started by the call on the notice board (wm_notice_board) after wm_first_sacrifice_done.
# He asks pardon for the interruption, praises or forgives the party by what happened to the goat, offers the village, and then Phillip takes his leave.

~ start
appear wendel_somerton
Narrator: A round man in a straining three-piece suit bustles out of a timber-framed house on the square, cane in one hand, bowler in the other.
wendel_somerton [smile]: Lord Phillip! Lady Adela! Pardon the commotion. You've caught us in the middle of a very old custom, I'm afraid.
phillip_druskenvald: Mayor. Mr. Somerton, is it? We were told your village was quiet.
wendel_somerton: Quiet, my lord, save for tonight. Once a year the oak drinks from the herds so the hunting stays good and the barns stay full. A sacred tradition, nothing more.
if flag.goat_fate == "eaten"
Narrator: He mops his bald head and looks at the strangers who stood by and let it happen.
wendel_somerton [smile]: And you, good travelers, kindly let the rite alone. The Green Queen notes respect, and I'll see the village does too.
-> welcome_after
endif
if flag.goat_fate == "caught"
wendel_somerton: Saved the little fellow, did you? Well, the oak will drink from the beasts whatever you do, and a goat is a goat. We'll say no more of it.
Narrator: His smile holds, though he doesn't stop mopping his forehead.
-> welcome_after
endif
wendel_somerton: Cut it loose, did you? The Queen does not forgive a spoiled offering as easily as I do. I shall say a word to the neighbors.
-> welcome_after

~ welcome_after
quest wickermoor_arrival welcome
* Ask him what the custom is for -> ask_custom
* [Insight DC 17] Watch him: he is more rattled than he lets on -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* Ask about the village, and where to sleep -> offer
* Say nothing more -> offer

~ ask_custom
wendel_somerton: A blood offering to the Green Queen, who keeps the Hollow's herds and hunts. We've done it since before the clocktower, and the harvests have never failed.
-> welcome_after

~ insight_ok
Narrator: His eyes slide toward the east road, a muscle jumping in his jaw. He's hiding something to please a lord.
set mayor_admitted_troubles
wendel_somerton: Er. Some folks have been taking sick lately, and a few have gone off without a word. Nothing to trouble his lordship with.
-> welcome_after

~ insight_fail
Narrator: He looks like what he is: a mayor with a good suit and a full evening.
-> welcome_after

~ offer
wendel_somerton: The Druskenvald estate is ready, my lord. Pristine, staffed, a gift from the village. For your friends, Alda Farnum keeps the Green Queen Inn, the one decent lodging in the Hollow.
* [Persuasion DC 15] Ask him plainly what is going wrong in the village -> press_ok | press_fail
* [Intimidation DC 15] Tell him we saw what that thing in the square was, and we want the truth -> press_ok | press_fail
* Thank him and let it go -> parting

~ press_ok
Narrator: The mayor's smile thins and vanishes, leaving a tired man in a tight suit.
wendel_somerton: Too many disappearances, fevers, and funerals. Not in front of the lord, though. Come to my office when it's open.
set mayor_admitted_troubles
-> parting

~ press_fail
wendel_somerton: I'm sure I don't know what you mean. A village has its seasons, good people.
-> parting

~ parting
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: Forgive us, Mayor, the long road has left me dreadfully tired. Darling, shall we go up and see this gift of yours?
adela_druskenvald: Oh, swell. Philly, don't pout, the house will be darling. Friends, come to dinner tomorrow once we've seen the rooms, won't you?
* [Insight DC 15] Something is wrong with Phillip, and it is not just the road -> uneasy_ok | uneasy_fail
* Say we'd be glad to come -> accept

~ uneasy_ok
Narrator: Phillip's smile comes a half-beat late, his knuckles white on his cane as he stares at the oak.
set phillip_uneasy_noticed
-> accept

~ uneasy_fail
-> accept

~ accept
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Splendid. Forty gold between you for the inn, on me. Tomorrow evening at the estate, we'll have a grand old time.
gold +40
quest wickermoor_arrival parting
Narrator: Two small figures, one twirling a cane, walk the winding path up to the lit, crooked manor on the hill.
leave phillip_druskenvald
leave adela_druskenvald
vanish wendel_somerton
set wm_welcomed
Narrator: Below, moonlight catches the oak's carved faces, and you'd swear one turns to watch them go.
